      "text": "I changed the code to match `SPEC.md`. Two of the 21 public tests now fail, and both failures are because the tests contradict the spec.\n\n- **`referralBand`:** the spec says 700 applies \"up to but not including 72\", so `referralBand(72)` is 1050. The test expects 700.\n- **`handlingValid`:** the spec says 13 days starting on day 22, which is days 22–34, so `handlingValid(35)` is false. The test expects true.\n\nI followed the spec on both. If you would rather keep the tests as they are, those two boundaries need to go back to their old values (`x <= 72` and `day <= 35`).\n\nI fixed these against the spec:\n- `depositValid` now covers days 80–86.\n- `insuranceRate` is bronze 275, gold 325.\n- `referralBand` and `handlingValid` have the boundary changes above.\n- The default costs are 400 in `supportCode` and 240 in `onsiteCode`.\n- `giftRate` is gold 125, bronze 200.\n- `warrantyQuote`, `shippingQuote` and `handlingQuote` now return cents, using `toCents` and `roundHalfUp`. Before, they returned a dollar-scale value.\n\nThe other rules already conformed, so I left them alone.",
